      {
        "id": "example",
        "type": "worked_example",
        "provenance": "original",
        "problem": {
          "en": "In triangle ABC, AB = 6, AC = 9, BC = 10 and AD bisects angle A with D on BC. Find BD and DC."
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "By the angle bisector theorem BD/DC = AB/AC = 6/9 = 2/3."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "The ratio is 2 : 3."
            }
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "Let BD = 2k and DC = 3k with 2k + 3k = 10."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "BD + DC = BC."
            }
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "en": "So k = 2, BD = 4 and DC = 6."
            },
            "why": {
              "en": "Check: 4/6 = 2/3."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "teachback",
        "type": "teach_back",
        "provenance": "original",
        "prompt": {
          "en": "Why does the bisector theorem not give BD = DC?"
        },
        "requiredIdeas": [
          {
            "en": "BD : DC equals AB : AC"
          },
          {
            "en": "BD = DC only when AB = AC"
          },
          {
            "en": "That is the isosceles case"
          }
        ],
